# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark data (large DWI datasets, not source)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark datasets and run outputs are large binary data - excluded.
# Git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so exclude its contents with
# `benchmark/*` instead; that lets the negations below re-include the harness,
# which is source and must not be dropped from a normal commit.
benchmark/*
# ALL of benchmark/ is excluded (owner's call, 2026-08-21). The datasets are ~114 GB
# and the harness travels with them rather than through git - it is useless without
# the data it drives. Copy the whole tree between machines. Previously scripts/,
# README.md, MANIFEST.json, LAST_REVALIDATE.json and END_TO_END_VARIABILITY.md were
# re-included; those negations are removed.
# benchmark/milestones/ is deliberately NOT re-included: the close-out documents are
# internal working evidence (M1-M6), like plan_*.md and audit_*.md below.

# EXCEPTION, added 2026-08-22: the harness IS re-included. The 2026-08-21 call assumed
# it was useless without the data; instead the Metal backend cases sat undelivered on
# one machine while another reported the harness could not drive Metal at all. The
# scripts are 236 KB of source and are how each backend is invoked - they must travel
# through git. Datasets and run outputs stay excluded.
!benchmark/scripts/

# Coding
plan_*.md
audit_*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output directories
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
build/
build*/
TORTOISEV4/build*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CMake artifacts (the README uses an in-source build: "cmake ." in TORTOISEV4/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeScripts/
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/
compile_commands.json
CMakeUserPresets.json
_deps/

# Generated makefiles / ninja files
Makefile
!src/**/Makefile
build.ninja
rules.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled objects, libraries and executables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.obj
*.lo
*.slo
*.ko
*.gch
*.pch
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.la
*.lai
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.d

# Static libraries are ignored, except the pre-built ones shipped with the repo
*.a
*.lib
!external_libraries/**/*.a
!src/external_src/**/*.a

# CUDA intermediates
*.cubin
*.fatbin
*.ptx
*.cu.o
*.cudafe*
*.gpu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
._*

# Python bytecode. measure_floor.py imports compare_outputs.py's directory, so
# scripts/ acquires a __pycache__ that the benchmark negations would otherwise
# re-include.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# per-run metadata trail (small, but data not source)
benchmark/*/*/history/

# Superseded by cuda_bug_demo/, which is the lean version written for upstream.
# Kept locally as the longer working write-up; not committed.
FieldFindMaxLocalNorm/
